{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"FIX MERGED. Gerrit change 2613 ('Answer e2e toolchain readiness under the lock', patchset 2 357182c8dcf0) reached LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 and was submitted; it is on main.\n\nTHE FIX: the pre-lock 'if _satisfied(...): return' is deleted. Readiness, the npm lookup and both\nprovisioning steps now run inside 'with _install_lock(js_dir):'.\n\nA SUBTLETY THAT WOULD HAVE BEEN A QUIET REGRESSION: the npm lookup had to move into the lock as well,\npositioned BELOW the readiness check. The old fast path returned before ever looking npm up, so\nleaving the lookup above the check would newly raise 'npm not on PATH' on an already-provisioned tree\nthat no longer has npm -- a case that previously worked fine. Covered by a dedicated test, and a\nsecond mutation hoisting the lookup back above the check kills that test.\n\nTHE REPRODUCTION IS DETERMINISTIC, which was the criterion that mattered most here and the one I\ninsisted on. Not N workers and hope: a child process takes the flock and WHILE HOLDING IT creates\nexactly what the unlocked check inspected -- node_modules/, node_modules/playwright/, and a\nhalf-written dist/roundtrip.mjs (esbuild writes in place, so the path exists long before the bytes\ndo) -- appends 'peer-mid-build', sleeps, appends 'peer-done', releases. The test blocks until\n'peer-mid-build' is on disk, which is a PRECONDITION rather than a race, then calls\nprovision_toolchain and appends 'caller-returned'. The append-only log is the oracle and the verdict\nis an ORDER, decidable in one run.\n\nRED against the unfixed code:\n  AssertionError: the caller returned while a peer still held the lock over a half-written bundle --\n  a readiness check ran outside the lock: ['peer-mid-build', 'caller-returned', 'peer-done']\nDefect-seeded mutation (restoring the pre-lock check with the fix in place) reproduces the identical\nfailure; reverted, module green.\n\nCardinality oracle for the uncontended path: cold single-worker 'pytest tests/e2e' over an empty\ntests/e2e/js gives 32 passed, and an npm shim on PATH logged EXACTLY TWO invocations -- 'ci' then\n'run build'. So the fix does not double-provision, which a naive move-everything-into-the-lock could\neasily have caused.\n\nCONTEXT: not a regression. Before change 2600 there was no lock at all and workers raced freely; 2600\nnarrowed the window and this closes the remainder. The two ACs carried over from the duplicate I\nmistakenly filed (c5ca, closed as duplicate) are both satisfied -- the deterministic reproduction and\nthe defect-seeded mutation proof."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788522208944461001,"uuid":"a071f957-29cd-4ef8-b348-d911a784b655"}